=== Text #1 ===
> [I] am a Thai (Indian origin),[ I] can help teach and transfer my Hindi language and the Indian culture to anyone willing to explore the language. The class will focus on speaking skills and can be[ altered] according to the students requirement. We can discuss a variation in the learning process as per the students requirement.[ I] also speak fluent English and Thai.
[I] specialize in teaching Hindi & English to students and adults.[ I] possess experience in teaching Hindi and English to University students.[ I] have taught children as part of the National Social Service Scheme in India.[ I] have a[ Doctor]ate degree and my academic career was supplemented by academic scholarship.[ I] have basic understanding of French. Its been one year since[ I] moved to Paris.[I] look forward to getting to know my students and helping them reach their goals in learning Hindi & English through innovative methods and cultural exploration!
Hello,[ I] am Asheesh.[ I] am Indian.[ My] mother tongue is Hindi.[ I] propose to teach Hindi depending on your requirement (Basic to Advanced) in easy way to help you learning it very fast.[ I] have experience in teaching languages. Basically,[ I] love teaching and[ I] enjoy it. If you are interested, don['t hesitate] to ask for availability. Thanks.
France is a big country and you may not live in Paris or[ T]oulouse, where you can find other Hindi-speaking Indians who might be interested in teaching their language and culture Indian.[ In] such cases,[ I] offer courses or conversations online, Hindi or Indian culture, whatever your need;[ I] am an Indian who has lived and worked in a high school in France as an English assistant, and[ I] am passionate about French language and culture.[ I] live in India now.
[I] have been teaching Hindi (Indian language) for several years. Teaching is my passion.[ It]'s my endeavor to help Hindi learners. We teach to meet with specific requirement of the learner.[ I] have already taught Hindi to few Hindi learners from France.
[I] have a very patient approach towards teaching and try to make the content and delivery specific to the requirements of the student.[ I] always try my level best to customize the session according to the requirement of the learner[ e]. g. the learner could be a foreign native and wish to learn Hindi for conversation because he has to make trips to India, or student lives outside India yet he/she is studying Hindi as a subject in his/her curriculum.[ In] both the cases, method of teaching would be entirely different.[ I] take one to one sessions, and the course content is designed as per requirements

=== Text #2 ===
> [I]'ve recently purchased the above model. It's very beautiful, robust and[ I] really like the 720p video it offers unlike the DCS-825L model.[ I]'ve set it up without problems in two Android phones and our Android tablet (all running Lollipop 5.0 and above).
The problem[ I] am facing is most probably with the camera itself.[ In] random times (it could be 2 hours, it could be 1 day) the camera will disappear from my wireless network.[ In fact],[ I] have[ noticed] that the camera reboots itself and when it finishes booting, the Green LED is on as it should be, but the blue (cloud)[ LED] start blinking slowly. After that[ I] cannot access the camera anymore and[ I] have to hard reset it and run the setup wizard all over again!
EDIT:[ I] just[ noticed] that if[ I] try to connect to the camera's web interface through a browser it says "File not found".[ Perhaps] the camera's[ firmware] is not installed correctly and therefore it randomly reboots?[ Is] there any way to reinstall the[ firmware]?
Wireless congested area:[ No]. Just a couple of other wireless networks around.
[I] hail from Europe, Greece![ I] hope you can make an exception and offer[ me] some help, since[ I] know this forum is only for US customers, as stated in the top of this page.
[I] don['t] think that DCS-855L has the capability of setting up a static IP.[ I] have even tried its web-interface (via http://[x].x.x.x/eng/mainFrame.cgi) and mydlink.com but[ i] don['t] see any relevant option.
Regarding the uPnP,[ I] have it enabled on my router.
Any other[ WiFi] routers in the area that[ maybe] causing interferences? Use a[ WiFi] Scanner to find out.[ How] many?
Try using Auto Channel Width and set a manual channel to 1, 6, 11 or[ 13]. Disable WPS and set Local[ Connection] only for IPv6 ON the router.
Set Auto Channel Width > Done.
Set to channel manually to[ 11] > Done.
... and set Local Connection only for IPv6 ON the router.
Regarding the above...[ I] have no[ idea what] it is and where to go τ[ο] set it[ I] found an option in Advanced Network "Enable IPv6 Multicast Streams" which was enabled.[ Is] this ok?
48 hours have passed and the camera works flawlessly![ I] have also set up an IP reservation

=== Text #3 ===
> [I]’m reading the Rust book in[ my] spare[ time] for some[ time] now and got to the topic of interior mutability.
Having a C++ background[ I] know similiar concepts from C++ as well like const_cast or mutable and[ I]’m really bugged by these things in C++ all the[ time] because it let’s you do things that you wouldn’t expect from the public API.
Every[time I] see constant methods in our code at work that uses some of these �[�]hacks” as[ I] call them to bypass the const mechanism it makes[ me] sick because it just doesn’t feels right to do these things.
[I] also never got any real use case for these hacks until[ I] read about interior mutability in the Rust book which showcases this feature in a unit testing-like scenario.
[I] never[ thought] about this so far but it kind of makes[ sense] to be able to do this in this specific scenario where the public API of some trait might get in the way.
Apart from that my[ mood] got worse as soon as[ I] read about Rust having these �[�]hacks” too.
So[ what I] really would like to know now is[ what] real world usecases there might be other than the unit testing scenario mentioned that really need interior mutability and cannot be solved in other ways?
Internal caching/[mem]oization is a prime use-case for interior mutability.[ When] you have[ obj].get_foo() and you want to compute the value laz[ily] and cache it internally without exposing that[ fact] in the API (using &[self], not &[mut self]). The way to �[�]cheat” that is interior mutability.
Another place where[ I] use it is in objects that are used in parallelized code.[ You] can’t use &[mut] foo across threads at all, but you can easily and cheaply share &foo between threads (scoped ones, like in Rayon). So[ Mut]ex or[ Rw]Lock in a struct allows having an object with all threading-friendly &[self] methods, but still some mutability.
BTW, they’re not hacks. They’re enforced to be correct at compile[ time]. If the public API says something can be called with a shared reference, then it safely can.
foo =[ 3]; // legal!
